 ## Operating characteristics
 - **Time Complexity:** $O(I J K p t |P|)$, where $I, J, K$ are the voxel grid dimensions, $p$ is samples per ray, $t$ is rays per column, and $|P|$ is the number of palette elements [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** Not given in the sources.
-- **Strengths:** Significantly reduces computation by treating empty/full voxels specially and using statistical checks. The column-based approach and ray-casting avoid expensive volumetric intersection tests [S1, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** Relies on stochastic sampling, so results may vary slightly between runs. The quality depends on the number of samples $t$ and $p$. The method assumes a two-manifold closed surface for the even intersection count [S1, unofficial].
-- **When to Use:** When voxelizing complex meshes with a palette of different shapes, and performance is critical. Suitable for applications where approximate geometric similarity is sufficient [S1, unofficial].
